      en: 'Ride east along the sand from Kuakata Zero Point and you reach Gangamati — one of the quietest and most natural stretches of the Kuakata coast. Rows of jhau (casuarina) and keora trees line the beach, and the wet sand is patterned with the tracks of countless red crabs.\n\nThis is the best place in Kuakata to watch the sunrise. As the eastern horizon reddens there is little noise beyond the surf and the wind in the trees. Walk up to the crabs and they vanish into their burrows; stand still at a distance and the whole beach seems to glow red.\n\nSea erosion eats into the tree line a little every year, and the uprooted trunks lying on the sand give the beach a striking, slightly wild look that photographers love.',
