      en: 'Near Jhalokathi town, the Gabkhan Channel is one of the most important waterways in Bangladesh. By linking the Sugandha and Sandhya rivers it shortens the inland shipping route between the Khulna–Mongla region and Barishal and Dhaka — which is why it is often called the “Suez Canal of Bengal”.\n\nThe tall Gabkhan Bridge (the Fifth Bangladesh–China Friendship Bridge) spans the channel and is a sight in its own right. Built high to let ships pass beneath, it offers wide views of rivers, canals and green villages in every direction.\n\nThe main pleasure here is simply watching the river traffic — cargo vessels, launches and trawlers moving through the channel — from the banks in the late afternoon. At sunset the water takes on a red glow and the scene is at its most beautiful.',
