      en: 'In the heart of Barishal town, beside Sadar Road, Bibir Pukur is a pond around two hundred years old. Local tradition says it was dug in the early nineteenth century by a woman named Jinnat Bibi to ease the water shortage of the townspeople, and it still carries her name.\n\nToday it is the city’s favourite meeting place. Paved banks and a walking path ring the water, and in the evening the lights come on and shimmer across the surface. Stalls selling fuchka, chotpoti and tea line the banks, and families, friends and evening walkers fill the area with life.\n\nIf you want a slice of everyday Barishal, an evening at Bibir Pukur is enough. It is also within easy reach of most other sights in town, making it a natural place to end a day of sightseeing.',
