      en: 'In Satla village of Uzirpur upazila, Barishal, a vast wetland bursts into bloom with thousands of red water lilies as the monsoon draws to a close. From a distance it looks as if a red carpet has been rolled out over the water, which is why Satla has become one of the best-known lily wetlands in Bangladesh.\n\nThe lilies are fully open at dawn and slowly close as the sun climbs. Gliding through them in a small dinghy at first light — with mist on the water and soft light for photographs — is the experience everyone comes for.\n\nFor local people the lilies are a livelihood as well as a sight: the stems are harvested and sold in markets as a vegetable. The season runs from about August to October, and an early start is essential.',
