      en: 'South of Rangabali upazila in Patuakhali, Sonar Char — “golden char” — sits out in the Bay of Bengal, named for the way its sand glitters gold in the midday sun. The island is fringed by mangrove forest planted by the Forest Department and is protected as a wildlife sanctuary.\n\nA long empty beach runs beside keora and gewa forest, the wet sand is alive with red crabs and seabirds wheel overhead — here nature far outnumbers people. Locals say that with luck you may see deer, monkeys or wild boar in the forest.\n\nGetting there is a little difficult, which keeps it free of crowds. Go between December and February, when the sea is calm; in the monsoon and cyclone season the crossing is genuinely dangerous.',
